From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zerollama <zerollama@local>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 02:28:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cpu: handle FP8 types in clamp switch

The native FP8 patches add E4M3 and E5M2 tensor types. Clamp does not
implement those formats, so classify them with the other unsupported
types instead of leaving the enum switch incomplete.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp
index 8e4feeb..e59bf0e 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp
@@ -5798,6 +5798,8 @@ void ggml_compute_forward_clamp(
                 ggml_compute_forward_clamp_f16(params, dst);
             } break;
         case GGML_TYPE_BF16:
+        case GGML_TYPE_FP8_E4M3:
+        case GGML_TYPE_FP8_E5M2:
         case GGML_TYPE_Q1_0:
         case GGML_TYPE_Q2_0:
         case GGML_TYPE_Q4_0:
